    "{"field":"promptTemplates","value":[{"id":"default-explain","name":"Explain code","body":"Explain how {{file or feature}} works: the main pieces, how data flows through them, and anything surprising. Don’t change any code."},{"id":"default-fix-bug","name":"Fix a bug","body":"Fix this bug: {{what happens and what should happen}}\\n\\nFind the root cause first, add a test that fails without the fix, then fix it and run the relevant tests."},{"id":"default-fix-issue","name":"Fix an issue","body":"Fix issue {{issue id}}. Read it in the issue tracker first (through its MCP server or CLI), find the root cause, add a test that fails without the fix, then fix it, run the relevant tests and open a pull request that references {{issue id}}."},{"id":"default-write-tests","name":"Write tests","body":"Write tests for {{file or feature}}. Follow the existing test conventions, cover edge cases and error paths, and run them."},{"id":"default-refactor","name":"Refactor","body":"Refactor {{file or feature}} to {{goal}} without changing its behavior. Keep the change focused and run the tests afterwards."},{"id":"default-review","name":"Review my changes","body":"Review the uncommitted changes in this workspace for bugs, regressions and missing edge cases. List concrete problems with file and line; skip style nitpicks."},{"id":"default-setup-repo","name":"Set up this repo","body":"Inspect this repository and propose a .foreman/settings.toml for it. Create or edit that one file in this workspace so the proposal shows up as a diff in Changes. Do not commit it, and do not change any other file.\\n\\nPropose only what you can justify from the repository itself (package.json scripts, Makefile, CI workflows, lockfiles, README, docs):\\n- [scripts] setup: the command a fresh checkout needs to become runnable (install dependencies).\\n- [[checks]]: name and command pairs for the tests, lint and typecheck commands the repo already uses (a command passes on exit code 0).\\n- sensitive_paths: globs for files a reviewer should look at closely (migrations, lockfiles, CI and deploy config, .env* templates, secrets-adjacent folders).\\n- Optionally a [scripts.run.dev] entry with a preview URL, if the repo has an obvious dev server.\\n\\nOnly read files while you inspect. Do not run commands that change the system or the project: no installs, builds, test runs, migrations, network calls, git writes or anything that starts a server. If something is unclear, leave it commented out with a note rather than guessing.\\n\\nThese settings are executable once applied, so finish by listing each command you proposed and where you found it, so I can review them before anything runs."}]}",
